# Laboratory #4: Build a Secure Login System with Testing
**Fintech Scenario | Phase 1: Design Documentation**[cite: 1]

This document outlines the architectural design, user flow, state management, and accessibility considerations for the secure fintech login system.

---

## 1. Sequence Diagram
The sequence diagram below demonstrates the secure authentication workflow, emphasizing input validation, prepared statements (preventing SQL injection), password hashing verification, and account lockout tracking.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Frontend as UI / Client
    participant Auth as Auth Controller
    participant DB as Secure Database

    User->>Frontend: Enter username & password
    Frontend->>Auth: POST /login (username, password)
    Auth->>Auth: Validate empty fields / Sanitize input
    alt Empty fields detected
        Auth-->>Frontend: Error: Fields cannot be empty
        Frontend-->>User: Display inline error
    else Input validated
        Auth->>DB: Query user via Prepared Statement (prevent SQLi)
        DB-->>Auth: Return user record (hash, attempts, lockout status)
        Auth->>Auth: Check account lockout status
        alt Locked Out
            Auth-->>Frontend: Error: Too many attempts. Account locked.
            Frontend-->>User: Display lockout notice + timer
        else Active Account
            Auth->>Auth: Verify password hash (Bcrypt)
            alt Password Match
                Auth->>DB: Reset failed_attempts = 0
                Auth-->>Frontend: Success: Session Token Issued
                Frontend-->>User: Redirect to Dashboard
            else Password Mismatch
                Auth->>DB: Increment failed_attempts + 1
                Auth-->>Frontend: Error: Invalid credentials
                Frontend-->>User: Display generic error message
            end
        end
    end
